        "title": "Show HN: Build with Python – a beginner course where your code draws",
        "link": "https://scimigo.com/en/learn/build-with-python/01-draw-with-python",
        "description": "<p>Hi HN, I built this because I watched my daughter struggle at learning Python. I made something that runs only in the browser with visuals rather than relying on CLI/terminal output. No need to worry about python installation, package versions, venv etc.<p>The lab runs with Pyodide in a web worker, and the program output is a picture by the side of the code block. A user would experiment with the code, and see the immediate changes in the visual output.<p>The course has 13 modules, with the first 6 foundation modules free, module 7-13 with free readings but guide labs for a one-time price of $49.<p>Please give it a try at <a href=\"https://scimigo.com/en/learn/build-with-python\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://scimigo.com/en/learn/build-with-python</a>\nSend me feedback on the UX and on the exercise design, especially if you teach kids to program.<p>I am also working on a C++ version for beginners (also with browser, no gcc or command lines). stay tuned.</p>\n<hr>\n<p>Comments URL: <a href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=49956771\">https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=49956771</a></p>\n<p>Points: 9</p>\n<p># Comments: 2</p>",
